<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p>Most trades get their work the same way: referrals, repeat customers and the odd job off a local Facebook group. It's a great way to run a business, right up until the referrals slow down and there's a gap in the diary you didn't see coming. The problem with word of mouth is you can't turn it up when you need it.</p>

      <h2>Why word of mouth isn't enough on its own</h2>
      <p>Referrals are unpredictable by nature. You can't schedule them, you can't scale them, and when a big job finishes you're back to hoping the phone rings. It's a brilliant thing to have alongside a system, but a risky thing to depend on. The trades who never worry about a quiet month are the ones who can generate leads on demand.</p>

      <h2>The system that actually works</h2>
      <p>For homeowner-facing trades in Scotland, the most dependable setup is Facebook ads run properly. Not boosting a post and hoping, but a proper system with three parts:</p>

      <h3>Local ads to homeowners</h3>
      <p>Targeted at homeowners in the exact postcodes you cover, so you're not paying to reach people you'd never travel to. Tight, local, and aimed at the people who actually turn into jobs.</p>

      <h3>Real footage of your work</h3>
      <p>Homeowners trust what they can see. Real clips of your actual jobs, the finish, the before-and-after, stop the scroll and build trust before anyone messages you. It beats a stock advert every single time.</p>

      <h3>A qualifying funnel</h3>
      <p>The ad clicks through to a page that asks the job, the postcode, the timeframe and the number, so tyre-kickers drop out and only serious homeowners reach your phone. This is the piece that turns clicks into leads worth quoting.</p>

      <h2>Then reply fast</h2>
      <p>The trade that replies first usually wins. So leads need to hit your phone the second they come in, with automated follow-up keeping them warm while you're on the tools. Speed turns a good lead into a booked job.</p>

      <h2>How to start</h2>
      <p>You don't need a website, and you don't need to become a marketer. You need the ads, the footage and the funnel set up properly around your trade, and the willingness to reply quickly. That's the system I build for trades across Scotland, from <a href="/industries/exterior-cleaning/">exterior cleaners</a> to <a href="/industries/kitchens/">kitchen fitters</a> to <a href="/industries/garage-conversions/">garage conversion companies</a>. <a href="/how-it-works/">Here's exactly how it works</a>, step by step.</p>

